&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, marketing, sales, and revenue teams to design and build AI-powered products and workflows that improve GTM efficiency and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the evolution of our growth platforms, including data pipelines, experimentation frameworks, and products used by teams and customers at Verkada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and integrate third-party solutions where appropriate, making thoughtful build vs. buy decisions grounded in impact and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an engineering architect by defining system design, making key technical decisions, and translating business goals into durable technical roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on through prototyping and targeted development to validate ideas, unblock progress, and maintain a deep understanding of the systems you lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience managing and developing engineering teams, including hiring, coaching, and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience as a software engineer, with demonstrated strength in designing scalable, reliable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering complex projects in an dynamic environment, balancing speed, quality, and long-term maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaborator who communicates clearly and builds alignment across technical and non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about emerging technologies—especially AI/ML—and how they can be applied to real GTM problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: experience with Python, SQL, AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: Familiarity with DAG-based workflow tools and data warehouses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
